<title>USA: Negotiated municipal sales total $549 mln Thursday.</title>
<headline>Negotiated municipal sales total $549 mln Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scheduled negotiated municipal bond sales are expected to total $549 million in eight offerings for Thursday, according to Reuters Municipal Bond Information Group.</p>
<p>The largest issue is a $375 million New York City Municipal Water Finance Authority deal through PaineWebber Inc.</p>
<p>An additional three negotiated deals totaling $17 million are on Reuter's possible calendar for Thursday, meaning underwriters have said they may price the issues depending on market conditions.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Information Group, 212-859-1826</p>
</text>
